    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1307">

                <pb facs="1259" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg973"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Guthrie</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-24T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of April 17, midnight. The Department shares sentiment of Baron
                    Sakatani opposing proposed economic alliance. You may say Department would
                    regret any combination which might restrict commerce between Japan and United
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
